INT. DEFUNCT PLANETARIUM - DOME CHAMBER - NIGHT

Dust hangs in a single flashlight beam. A cracked star projector squats at the center like a dead insect.

INES MARCHETTI (30s, lean, gloved) kneels at the projector's base, a drill whining in her hands. TOBY WREN (20s, nervous, oversized hoodie) holds the light and keeps glancing at the exit. KOFI ADEYEMI-BELL (50s, broad, patient) feeds cable from a spool through a panel in the floor.

INES
Hold it still.

TOBY
I am holding it still.

INES
You're holding it like a wet cat.

The drill bites through. A brass plate drops and rings across the floor. All three freeze.

A RADIO crackles on Kofi's belt.

NIGHT GUARD (V.O.)
(over radio, bored)
Dome's quiet. Any of you hear that?

Kofi thumbs the key slowly.

KOFI
(into radio, flat)
Pipes. Same as every night.

NIGHT GUARD (V.O.)
Copy. Pipes.

Kofi releases the key. Toby exhales. Ines does not look up.

INES
Cable.

Kofi passes the cable. Ines threads it into the hole, seats the connector, and the projector's casing opens with a sigh. Inside, wrapped in velvet, a silver sphere the size of a grapefruit.

TOBY
That's it?

INES
That's it.

Toby reaches. Ines slaps his wrist. Boots echo in the corridor outside. The three of them kill the light and drop flat behind the projector. Kofi pulls the velvet over the sphere with one hand and presses Toby's head down with the other.

NIGHT GUARD (V.O.)
(over radio, closer)
Dome, this is Marsh. I'm at the door.

The door handle turns. Ines slides a blade from her sleeve. Toby grabs Kofi's sleeve. Kofi quietly lifts a fire extinguisher off the floor, and the three of them hold their breath as the door swings inward half a foot, a wedge of hallway light cutting across the carpet and stopping inches from Ines's boot.

NIGHT GUARD (V.O.)
(muttering)
Pipes.

The door closes. Footsteps fade.

KOFI
(whisper)
Ninety seconds. Then we move.

INES
Sixty.

They scatter toward the loading dock, the sphere gone, the dome black.
